# Arch Rice Installer

This repository contains a minimal one-command installer that sets up the same theme and shell base as your current KDE/KWin + Noctalia configuration.

## One command

```bash
bash <(curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/BlackoneBc/arch-rice/main/install.sh)
```

## What it sets up
- Plymouth with `cachyos` theme
- SDDM with the `silent` theme
- KWin session entry: `KWin Noctalia`
- KDE theme values matching your current system
- Cursor: `Bibata-Modern-Classic`
- Icons: `Mint-Y-Yaru`
- Window decoration: `WillowDark`
- Qt/KDE look: `Breeze Dark`
- GTK settings and cursor configuration
- Noctalia config and KWin session entry
- Spicetify + Marketplace theme
- Flatpak Spotify + GNOME Software + Pamac

## Included config files
- `config/kdeglobals`
- `config/kwinrc`
- `config/kglobalshortcutsrc`
- `config/plasmarc`
- `config/gtk-3.0/settings.ini`
- `config/gtk-4.0/settings.ini`
- `config/noctalia/settings.json`
- `config/noctalia/colors.json`
- `config/noctalia/plugins.json`
- `config/spicetify/config-xpui.ini`

## Notes
This installer intentionally focuses on the exact theme stack and shell setup you want, without trying to reproduce the full software universe of a desktop environment.

It is designed to be used on a fresh Arch installation and then let the user log into the KWin Noctalia session.

